Sval: Mozilla's FPP matrix tests skip private windows for granular entries

fp-overrides-private-scope keeps the entries in the granular-overrides prefs
out of private windows, because those prefs hold choices made in normal
windows. browser_fpp_protections_matrix_2 to _4 expect such entries to apply
in private windows too, so the private-window check of a case whose
expectation comes from a granular entry is skipped. The rest of each case
still runs.

